@startuml
' Phase 9 — Job Learning: planned infrastructure. Authored at phase start.
' Copy to summary.uml at phase end and edit to the as-built state.

title Phase 9 — Job Learning (planned)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "aa-kernel (Go; imports contracts + obsv + memory + toolbox)" as kernel {
  component "telemetry (bounded evidence + deterministic candidates)" as telemetry
  component "orchestrator / gate (cycle + gate outcomes)" as cycle
  component "registry (roles, trades, workers)" as registry
  component "joblearn (types + errors + clock)" as core
  component "joblearn.attribution (attribute + versioned scoring)" as attribution
  component "joblearn.candidates (patterns, pitfalls, strategies, hints)" as candidates
  component "joblearn.similarity (feature clusters + conflict)" as similarity
  component "joblearn.gate (capability registry + evidence gates)" as gate
  component "joblearn.backtest (baseline comparison + budget)" as backtest
  component "joblearn.route (hint + deterministic fallback)" as route
  component "joblearn.promote (Sink -> memory candidates)" as promote
}

package "aa-memory (canonical store + promotion)" as memory {
  component "repo (lifecycle transitions; typed memory-record repository)" as repo
}

package "aa-contracts (memory_record, strategy, telemetry, route v1)" as contracts
package "aa-obsv (scaffolded; observation evidence deferred)" as obsv
package "aa-sifter (deterministic recommender baseline; RPC deferred)" as sifter
package "aa-console (reports surface, later)" as console

contracts --> core
telemetry --> attribution
cycle --> attribution
registry --> attribution
attribution --> candidates
candidates --> similarity
attribution --> similarity
candidates --> gate
similarity --> gate
attribution --> backtest
gate --> backtest
backtest --> route
gate --> route
candidates --> promote
gate --> promote
promote --> repo : CANDIDATE records (Sink)
repo --> repo : Transition (VALIDATED/ACTIVE)
obsv ..> attribution : observation evidence (deferred)
sifter ..> backtest : deterministic baseline (fake now; RPC later)
console ..> backtest : evaluation reports (later)

note right of telemetry
  ADR-P9-002: attribution and
  scoring consume bounded evidence
  (telemetry, gate outcomes, history)
  and are deterministic; no model is
  called anywhere in the loop.
end note

note bottom of candidates
  ADR-P9-008: every candidate carries
  provenance, a level, and
  applicability. ADR-P9-001: the
  kernel proposes; memory owns
  canonical state and promotion.
end note

note bottom of similarity
  ADR-P9-003: similarity is
  feature-based and deterministic
  (no embeddings); conflicts are
  detected per scope, independent of
  input order.
end note

note bottom of gate
  ADR-P9-004/005: capabilities are
  disabled by default. Enablement
  requires enough attributed outcomes
  and a backtest win over the
  deterministic baseline.
end note

note bottom of backtest
  ADR-P9-005: a candidate policy is
  compared to a baseline over a
  bounded dataset; the report is
  deterministic and budgeted.
end note

note bottom of route
  ADR-P9-006/007: the learned signal
  is a hint only; a deterministic
  fallback is always returned, and a
  human gate or execution contract is
  never bypassed.
end note

note bottom of repo
  ADR-P9-001/009: candidates persist
  as CANDIDATE via the shared
  promotion transitions; promotion
  stays explicit and evidence-gated.
end note

@enduml
